			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Implement real idle detection and power-save blocker shims\n\nMTN-15/16: Query CGEventSourceSecondsSinceLastEventType on macOS for\nactual keyboard/mouse idle time. Returns 'idle' after 60s and millisecond\nprecision idle duration. Non-macOS falls back to 'unknown'/0.\n\nMTN-17: Increment power-save blocker IDs atomically so start/stop pair\ncorrectly. Stop always returns true.\n\nMTN-18/40: Parse URI into UriComponents {scheme, authority, path, query,\nfragment} for env:asExternalUri and env:resolveExternalUri. VS Code's\nUri.revive() destructures these fields — returning only {uri} caused\nundefined field errors.",
			"SHA": "2efd9e2c634e11c19cf7126fd89c9ad32437d810"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:47:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Nest tokio::spawn for fully detached editor state notifications\n\nThe per-keystroke editor state notifications (selection, active editor, visible editors, tabs, ranges, options, diff, viewColumn) were already dispatched via `tokio::spawn` to move them off the IPC dispatch queue, but the outer spawn still owned the Vine gRPC future until `SendNotification::Fn` completed. Nest a second `tokio::spawn` inside each handler so the outer task returns immediately after scheduling the inner task, decoupling the IPC handler's completion from the gRPC call's execution entirely.\n\nEliminates the final serialization point in the editor:event dispatch pipeline for all 8 notification types.",
			"SHA": "523b43a4c3eec376ddb65de8571a0b9a14246c3d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:46:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Return LogLevel for logger:getLevel, cache TierIPC\n\n`logger:getLevel` was matching a stubbed null-returning arm in two places, but VS Code's Logger service expects a numeric LogLevel enum (Trace=0 through Critical=5). The TierIPC env var was read from the OS on every unknown command dispatch.\n\nRemove `logger:getLevel` from both null-returning stubs and add a dedicated handler returning `json!(log::max_level() as u32)`. Cache the TierIPC lookup in a `OnceLock` so the syscall and allocation run once.\n\nVS Code can now query the current log level through the VS Code LogLevel API. Fallthrough command dispatch overhead is reduced by one env lookup per call.",
			"SHA": "f0488344a0976a0be537568a9a7c95485333821c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:43:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				3
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Fire-and-forget Cocoon notifications for editor state events\n\nConvert 8 synchronous SendNotification calls in the sky:editor:* handler group to `tokio::spawn` so selection, active, visible, tabs, ranges, options, diff, and viewColumn change notifications no longer block the IPC dispatch queue on Vine gRPC RTT. These fire at per-keystroke/scroll frequency and were a serial bottleneck in the command handler.\n\nAdd `sky://editor/active-changed` Tauri event emission as the canonical renderer-side event, enabling Wind's Editor layer to track active editor changes through native event channels rather than gRPC.\n\nAdd `tasks:` and `auth:` command guards to the tier-routing gates, forwarding both families to Cocoon when their tier flags indicate Node dispatch — consistent with the existing debug and encryption gates.\n\nIn InitializationData.rs, add `codeCachePath`, `autoDetectHighContrast`, `accessibilitySupport`, and `isInitialStartup` to ISandboxConfiguration — the bundled workbench accesses these without null guards, and their absence caused V8 code-cache load failures and INativeWindowConfiguration contract crashes.",
			"SHA": "57366f3f7c60054355ffa963ed2d6455609db376"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:39:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				3
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Revise Architecture and DeepDive opening sections for direct narrative style\n\nReplace the meta-textual framing \"This document describes\" in Architecture.md with a direct statement that positions Mountain as the primary Tauri application. Reword the DeepDive.md opening paragraph to move the document's purpose into a supporting clause rather than the lead, bringing Mountain's concrete role as the VSCode service implementation layer to the forefront.\n\nEliminates redundant document-self-reference prose across both documentation files.",
			"SHA": "dbc2afc52dc28939909ca893a87774ed13ea8169"
		}
	],
